# Starter egress allowlist: the hosts Claude Code needs. Copy it to
# ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/csb/allowed-hosts, where csb reads it under
# --filter-egress. It is also what `make proxy-run` serves by default.
#
# Derived from Anthropic's documented network requirements, not guessed:
# https://code.claude.com/docs/en/network-config
# Rationale per host, and the droppable ones, are in
# docs/PLAN-009-proxy.md section 9a.
#
# Format: one host per line; `#` comments and blank lines ignored. A leading
# `*.` matches subdomains only, so list a bare parent domain separately when it
# is also wanted.
#
# These entries are add-only: they union with --allow-host and any config
# layer's allow_host=. The file is read once per launch, so an edit applies to
# the next one.

# --- required -----------------------------------------------------------------
# API requests, WebFetch domain safety check, feature flags.
api.anthropic.com
# OAuth token exchange, refresh and revocation. Required even for claude.ai
# sign-ins -- omitting it yields a session that dies when the token expires.
platform.claude.com

# --- required when seeding host session credentials (--seed-creds) ------------
claude.ai

# --- recommended: documentation lookups --------------------------------------
# claude-code-guide and pre-approved WebFetch requests.
code.claude.com
claude.com

# --- optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# /release-notes changelog feed.
raw.githubusercontent.com
# Plugin metadata for /plugin; signed artifact uploads.
storage.googleapis.com

# --- opt in if you use claude.ai MCP connectors ------------------------------
# claude.ai-hosted MCP connectors (mcp__claude_ai_* tools) route through this
# host; with it denied they fail. Uncomment to enable them, or set
# ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS=false so nothing attempts it.
# mcp-proxy.anthropic.com

# This list assumes the companion env below. Without it claude ATTEMPTS the
# omitted hosts and surfaces a denial as a user-visible error -- a measured
# example: denying downloads.claude.ai produces a persistent
# "Auto-update failed - Run claude doctor" banner. Keep the two in sync, or a
# tight allowlist trains you to ignore real errors.
#
#   DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1                        # downloads.claude.ai
#   CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC=1   # the datadoghq.com hosts
#   ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS=false            # mcp-proxy.anthropic.com
#                                                # (omit if you want connectors)
#
# Deliberately NOT listed (see section 9a). Each was OBSERVED being attempted
# and denied in a real session (2026-08-06):
#   downloads.claude.ai            update check; csb pins claude via nix, so an
#                                  update would target a read-only store path
#   http-intake.logs.us5.datadoghq.com   telemetry
#   mcp.us5.datadoghq.com          telemetry; NOT in Anthropic's documented
#                                  host table -- found only by running this
# Documented but never attempted here:
#   browser-intake-us5-datadoghq.com  error reports (rollout-gated)
#   formulae.brew.sh               homebrew installs only
#   registry.npmjs.org             npm/bun installs only
#   bridge.claudeusercontent.com   Claude in Chrome
